{
    "word": "sorehead",
    "lang_code": "en",
    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "2d88f093-35b4-3312-a13c-e76475611b77",
                "word": "sorehead",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "7a9ea374-265b-4434-afa0-188fa70162db",
                        "entry_id": "2d88f093-35b4-3312-a13c-e76475611b77",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "soreheads"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ffaa18d7-eb31-3f40-959a-c7cff280e23c",
                        "entry_id": "2d88f093-35b4-3312-a13c-e76475611b77",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A person who has a tendency to be angry or to feel offended."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8a5474fb-cec4-4fab-b000-140b567d9964",
                                "sense_id": "ffaa18d7-eb31-3f40-959a-c7cff280e23c",
                                "text": "Don't be a sorehead! Forgive, forget and get on with your life."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "72ebd78b-7e37-4608-a96b-18baa92f8293",
                                "sense_id": "ffaa18d7-eb31-3f40-959a-c7cff280e23c",
                                "text": "Of course, my competitive nature occasionally crossed the line into being a sorehead and poor loser."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2d40441f-ea2d-4078-a550-c482ffe7016e",
                                "sense_id": "ffaa18d7-eb31-3f40-959a-c7cff280e23c",
                                "text": "2000, Nancy Capace, McGill, Ralph Emerson, entry in Encyclopedia of Tennessee, page 63,\nHe antagonized them by printing that they were a bunch of \"failures . . . chronic soreheads . . . hoodlums, and toughs who have no faith in themselves.\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e570c5c4-5173-4296-ae8f-7a6cd071a901",
                                "sense_id": "ffaa18d7-eb31-3f40-959a-c7cff280e23c",
                                "text": "No matter what the size or type of community, you'll have critics, and they are not always just soreheads who are unhappy when a team loses."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5295fea5-8888-3644-84c5-8b5e297079c5",
                        "entry_id": "2d88f093-35b4-3312-a13c-e76475611b77",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A politician who is dissatisfied through failure, lack of recognition, etc."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "US",
                            "countable",
                            "derogatory",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "afa0b364-de83-40fc-9fbe-3a0ba5e9c642",
                                "sense_id": "5295fea5-8888-3644-84c5-8b5e297079c5",
                                "text": "In most of these areas there was improvement between 1920, the year of the second Farmer-Labor ballot and the last election in which the coalition was able to use sorehead tactics, and the special senatorial election of 1923."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2c548a07-182a-4231-837c-04cb2e161105",
                                "sense_id": "5295fea5-8888-3644-84c5-8b5e297079c5",
                                "text": "Officials walked a tightrope because disappointed voters could join or, if need he, form an opposing coalition, and they could cozy up to \"soreheads\" who were encouraging merger with Chicago."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "708de383-d06c-49b4-bac9-df511bbc48fe",
                                "sense_id": "5295fea5-8888-3644-84c5-8b5e297079c5",
                                "text": "2007, Bessie Louise Pierce, A History of Chicago, Volume III: The Rise of a Modern City, 1871-1893, page 341,\nDespite the opposition of professional politicians of unsavory reputation and men the Tribune described as “irresponsible soreheads,” the Medill ticket swept into office with a flatteringly large vote."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6ad04497-36ee-397d-b89b-7892514e2ee6",
                        "entry_id": "2d88f093-35b4-3312-a13c-e76475611b77",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Infection in sheep by the nematode Elaeophora schneideri; elaeophorosis."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c500eedb-879e-41bb-bbbc-3a33ab72cc63",
                                "sense_id": "6ad04497-36ee-397d-b89b-7892514e2ee6",
                                "text": "And sometimes, the bugs themselves are the predators, the killers and consumers of elk.\nI think of the green-headed horsefly and its bloody conspirator, the sorehead roundworm—Elaeophora schneideri."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "586d4da5-56cd-43f3-bd9b-e3bc7b1cdf55",
                                "sense_id": "6ad04497-36ee-397d-b89b-7892514e2ee6",
                                "text": "2012, D. G. Pugh, N. (Nickie) Baird, Sheep and Goat Medicine, unnumbered page,\nElaeophora schneideri is a filarial nematode that has been reported primarily in wildlife species in the western United States, including mule deer and bighorn sheep. Elaeophorosis (sorehead) is uncommon in sheep and goats."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "65c66747-71d0-3698-83f2-8504d4bb8547",
                        "entry_id": "2d88f093-35b4-3312-a13c-e76475611b77",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Fowlpox."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b9112184-6472-41ac-952e-b60822c1296a",
                                "sense_id": "65c66747-71d0-3698-83f2-8504d4bb8547",
                                "text": "Sorehead is a prevailing trouble in Hawaii, but I am convinced that much sorehead, if not all of it, can be averted if we keep our chicks off the ground until they are at least three months old."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cec56290-46dc-47e9-aebc-1f15aecaee66",
                                "sense_id": "65c66747-71d0-3698-83f2-8504d4bb8547",
                                "text": "1922, University of Hawaii (Honolulu), Agricultural Dept, Annual Report of the Agricultural Department, Volume 4, page 103,\nThe two principal causes of death among chicks has been sorehead and coccidiosis."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "27784032-a7c5-4476-94f1-485a8a7754e1",
                                "sense_id": "65c66747-71d0-3698-83f2-8504d4bb8547",
                                "text": "Such ailments as sorehead and pip also took their toll. Children learned early not to throw watermelon rinds where the chickens could peck them: pecking watermelon rinds gave chickens sorehead."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "135c1940-9c9a-4d20-9252-eb9e497e6421",
                        "source_entry_id": "2d88f093-35b4-3312-a13c-e76475611b77",
